  "disease_label_per_paper": "Shiga toxin-associated hemolytic uremic syndrome associated with Escherichia coli O157:H7 infection in an older adult",
  "expected_manifold": "D-STEC-HUS",
  "demographics": {
    "age": 86,
    "sex": "F"
  },
  "presentation_summary": [
    "86-year-old woman presented with acute abdominal pain, bright red blood per rectum, breathing difficulty, altered mental status, and speech difficulty.",
    "CT abdomen suggested colitis and she received levofloxacin and metronidazole before transfer.",
    "She had purpura/ecchymoses, respiratory failure requiring intubation, MAHA, thrombocytopenia, high LDH, very low haptoglobin, renal failure, and coagulopathy markers that were not classic DIC.",
    "She was treated empirically as TTP with plasma exchange and methylprednisolone while awaiting ADAMTS13 and Shiga-toxin assays, and underwent hemodialysis.",
    "Normal ADAMTS13 and stool STEC/E. coli O157:H7 culture confirmed STEC-HUS; plasma exchange and steroids were stopped, but she died on the fourth hospitalization day at the reporting institution."
  ],
